<p>Note 1. -- The Detroit News and the Detroit Free Press operate under a joint operating agreement as the Detroit Newspaper Agency (DNA).  Revenue, linage and circulation for 1996 and 1995 include 50% of the DNA.  1996 and 1995 results reflect the impact of the Detroit strike, as we have now cycled through a full year.</p>
<p>Note 2. -- Knight-Ridder owns 49.5% of the voting stock and 65% of the non-voting common stock of the Seattle Times. Full-run ROP linage of the Joint Operating Agency between the Seattle Times and the Seattle Post Intelligencer was 254 for the period (even with the prior year) and 2,343 for the year to date (down 9.6% from the prior year). Revenue, circulation and linage for 1996 and 1995 are not included in this report.</p>
